If you go to extra effort to properly estimate them!  See the section on 
imputation using
the Hmisc library in the document by Alzola & Harrell on our web page for an 
example
in which the bootstrap is used to estimate the covariances correctly by putting 
imputation
inside the bootstrap loop.  This is not computationally feasible for transcan 
(customized
imputation models) but I'm working on it.

