Hello Steve,

There's also an easy way to get asymptotic 
confidence limits:

Spearman's correlation coefficient results by plugging the 
ranks of the two variables into the formula of the "normal"
Pearson correlation coefficient. 

Thus,  first calculate ranks, second calculate for the ranks 
the Pearson correlation coefficient and get by the way the
confidence limits, you're interested in.

