machine you will have, 128 mb ram and a good processor, nt is
the way to go. I've run Splus on my work machine (nt) and my home
machine (95) and have found that nt is significantly faster and less
prone to any programs crashing. If you (only) have 16 or 32 mb ram, I
would say that 95 is a good option since it will suck up less ram. Using
the Performance Monitor in nt while running Splus, I've seen anywhere
from 15% to 100% of cpu resources being used. nt tends to need about 16%
