From: mueter at halibut.ims.uaf.edu (Franz-Josef Mueter)
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 1998 16:35:18 -0900
Subject: Re: [S] Q: How to sum the diagonals of a matrix?
In-Reply-To: <9803198903.AA890312311@ssagw07.ssa.gov>
References: <9803198903.AA890312311@ssagw07.ssa.gov>
Message-ID: <Pine.SUN.3.91.980319163039.10079A-100000@halibut.ims.alaska.edu>

A simple way to do it is to use row(x)+col(x), which will return
appropriate indices, with tapply: 

> x <- matrix(1:20,4)
> x                  
     [,1] [,2] [,3] [,4] [,5] 
[1,]    1    5    9   13   17
[2,]    2    6   10   14   18
[3,]    3    7   11   15   19
[4,]    4    8   12   16   20

> tapply(x,col(x)+row(x),sum)
 2 3  4  5  6  7  8  9 
 1 7 18 34 50 45 35 20

will give the desired result

